2026/11/18 1:15
Version 8.1 change summary
Based on version 7.0, I had the AI generate a new version 8.1 metric calculation protocol.

Changes in Version 8.1:
================================================================
In order to reduce LLM inference time, I prevented it from generating files other than essential ones.

2026/11/18 0:51
Version 8.0 change summary
Without being based on version 7.0, I had the AI generate a completely new version 8.0 metric calculation protocol.

Changes in Version 8.0:
================================================================
1. Rebuilt the evaluation protocol from scratch as a standalone procedure.
2. Expanded the workflow to 12 phases, prioritizing accuracy over execution speed.
3. Made LLM-based semantic entailment analysis mandatory.
4. Restricted keyword matching, TF-IDF, and similarity scores to evidence retrieval.
5. Strengthened atomic claim extraction and excluded non-normative statements.
6. Required complete semantic deduplication across all eight specifications.
7. Separated expected cross-document reuse from redundant duplication.
8. Strengthened TP verification using direct evidence, universal rules, contextual applicability, and cross-document reasoning.
9. Strengthened FN verification through exhaustive bidirectional evidence searches.
10. Required PDF-grounded validation of every generated claim before confirming FP.
11. Introduced two-pass semantic FP consolidation to prevent duplicate counting.
12. Separated unresolved judgments from confirmed FP and FN.
13. Prohibited automatically counting unresolved claims as FP.
14. Required uncertainty ranges instead of misleading definitive metrics.
15. Strengthened critical-decision review and independent adjudication requirements.
16. Preserved the frozen Gold Set and negative controls without modification.
17. Required complete evidence provenance and traceable judgment corrections.
18. Added strict cross-file reconciliation and independent metric recomputation.
19. Prevented incomplete semantic evaluations from receiving verified status.
20. Removed the fixed six-turn deadline and required each phase to satisfy its acceptance criteria before proceeding.

2026/11/18 23:02
Version 7.0 change summary
Without being based on version 6.2, I had the AI generate a completely new version 7.0 metric calculation protocol.

OrionDesk Atomic Evaluation Protocol v6.2 — Problems and Solutions in v7.0
================================================================
1. Problem: The Gold Set could be modified during metric evaluation.
Solution: Freeze the Gold Set before evaluation and prohibit all modifications.
2. Problem: Gold Set construction and validation were mixed with metric evaluation.
Solution: Remove both processes entirely from the evaluation protocol.
3. Problem: Gold Set completeness could not be guaranteed.
4. Problem: Semantically duplicate false positives could inflate FP counts.
Solution: Strengthen semantic FP deduplication across all generated specifications.
5. Problem: TP and FP used different counting units.
Solution: Retain conventional Precision, Recall, and F1, and introduce Generated Claim Validity Rate (GCVR) as a separate auxiliary metric.
6. Problem: Duplicate metrics did not distinguish legitimate reuse from unnecessary repetition.
Solution: Classify duplicates as EXPECTED_REUSE or REDUNDANT_DUPLICATE.
7. Problem: Excessive processing requirements could increase human interaction.
Solution: Limit evaluation to six turns, completing one phase per turn without restricting internal LLM operations.
8. Problem: Critical LLM judgments lacked independent verification.
Solution: Require one independent review and at most one targeted resolution for each critical decision or equivalent group.
9. Problem: Confirmed and unconfirmed false negatives were not sufficiently distinguished.
Solution: Report TRUE_FN and UNCONFIRMED_FN separately, while including both in total FN.
10. Problem: TN could be misinterpreted as representing all possible true negatives.
Solution: Explicitly restrict TN to the fixed, bounded negative-control set.

